    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 5.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.5" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.30"/><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe stalað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.31"/> on Sunnanniht oððe on Gehhol<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.32"/> oððe on Eastron oððe on ðone halgan Þunresdæg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.33"/> on Gangdagas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.34"/>: ðara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.35"/> gehwelc we willað sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.36"/> twybote, swa on Lenctenfæsten.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe stalað on Sunnonniht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.3"/> oþþe on Geohhol<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.9"/> oððe on Eastron oþþe on ðone halgan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.10"/> Ðunresdæg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.11"/> on Gongdagas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.3"/>: þara æghwylc we willaþ sy twybote, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.12"/> Lenctenfæsten.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.5" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe stalað ón Sunnanniht oðð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.4"/> on Geol oððe on Eastron oððe on ðone halgan Þunresdæg ⁊ on Gangdagas: ðara g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>hwylc we willað, sy twybote, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.5"/> on Lenctenfæsten.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui furatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.13"/> die dominica uel in sancto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.14"/> natali uel in pascha uel in sancto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.15"/> die Iouis in ascensione Domini: in quolibet eorum uolumus dupliciter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.16"/> emendandum sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.oe.14"/>, sicut in quadragesimali ieiunio.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="66" ed="#attenborough"/>Se ðe stalað on Sunnanniht oððe on Gehhol<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Af_5-5.attnote.fn.16"/> oððe on Eastron oððe on ðone halgan Þunresdæg on<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Af_5-5.attnote.fn.17"/> Gangdagas: ðara gehwelc<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Af_5-5.attnote.fn.18"/> we willað sie twybote, swa on Lenctenfæsten.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="6" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="298" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Se ðe staleð on Sunnanniht oððe on Gehhol oððe on Eastron oððe on ðone halgan Ðunresdæg on Gangdagas: ðara gehwelc we willað sie twybote, swa on Lenctenfæsten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer stiehlt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.de.1"/> am Sonntage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.de.2"/> oder zu Weihnachten oder zu Ostern oder am heiligen Donnerstag<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.de.3"/> in den Betfahrtstagen: deren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.de.4"/> jeder stehe, wollen wir, in Doppelbusse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_5-5.lnote.de.5"/>, ebenso wie zu Frühlingsfasten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever steals on Sunday or at Christmas or at Easter or on Holy Thursday in Rogation Days: each of these, we wish, is to be subject to double compensation, just as in the Lenten fast.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="67" ed="#attenborough"/>We decree that he who steals on Sunday<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_5-5.attnote.n.1"/>, or during Christmas or Easter, or on Holy Thursday, at Rogation Days<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_5-5.attnote.n.2"/>, shall pay in each case double compensation, just as he must [if he steals] during Lent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="411" ed="#whitelock"/>Whoever steals on Sunday or at Christmas or Easter or on the Holy Thursday in Rogation days; each of those we wish to be compensated doubly, as in the Lenten fast.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="299" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who steals on Sunday (night) or on Christmas or on Easter or on Holy Thursday [or] during Rogation Days: each of those [offenses] we wish to count two-fold, as in the Lenten fast.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_47">II Cn 47</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_40-2">Af 40.2</ref> <quote>5:5 (ref. 40:2)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="299"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9</ref> <quote>the time period seems to be Sunday reckoned as the Sabbath in Jewish law [...] see McReavy 1935: 320, also Wihtred §8 [L9].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><ref target="clause:IICn_47">II Cn 47</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="469"><ref target="clause:IICn_47">II Cn 47</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in Ld steht</hi> 5, 5 <hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> 6, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in Ld 5, 5 comes after 6, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">stæl. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">stæl. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geol <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geol Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dæge <hi rend="italic">So Ld;</hi> oððe <hi rend="italic">fügt zu So;</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dæge So Ld; oððe added by So; ⁊ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gum <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gum So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæra gehwylce <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæra gehwylce Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy twybôt <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy twybôt Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geol, <hi rend="italic">am Rande vom Textschreiber:</hi> al. geohhol.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geol, in the margin by the text scribe: al. geohhol.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur vor</hi> g</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure before g</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">über der Linie zugefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ added above the line</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur 2 Buchst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure of 2 letters</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">furantur <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">furantur Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in s. d. J. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in s. d. J. lacking in Hk Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">duplo <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">duplo Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">al <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. davor geschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">al written before it in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Feiertag 9. Rauferei in der Bittwoche zu London fällt im 12. Jh. unter ‘Kronprozess’; ed. Bateson in <hi rend="italic">EHR</hi> 1902, 494</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Feiertag 9. In the 12th cent. brawling in Rogation week in London falls under ‘pleas of the Crown’; ed. Bateson in <hi rend="italic">EHR</hi> 1902, 494</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Nacht von Sonnabend auf Sonntag’ (Toller); dies wäre <hi rend="italic">sunnan æfen</hi> Wi 9. Hier ist der ganze Sonntag gemeint; <hi rend="italic">niht</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 2) bed. 24 Stunden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘the night from Saturday to Sunday’ (Toller); that would be <hi rend="italic">sunnan æfen</hi> Wi 9. Here the whole Sunday is meant; <hi rend="italic">niht</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> 2) means 24 hours</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘und’ fügt zu B H cor., ‘oder’ So, irrtümlich. Die Prozessionstage in 5. Woche nach Ostern bereiten vor auf Christi Himmelfahrt; um Hof, Vieh und Flur trägt man Kreuz, Evangelien, Reliquien; Agsä. Predigt um 1000 ed. M. Förster in <hi rend="italic">Morsbach Festg.</hi> 74. <hi rend="italic">‘Holy Thursday’</hi> ohne Weiteres heisst ‘Himmelfahrt’ zwar Mittelenglisch und jetzt. Dagegen Agsächs. bedarf es zu dieser Bed. der näheren Bestimmung (= altfrz. <hi rend="italic">joedi de rovoisons</hi> bei Littré s. v. <hi rend="italic">jeudi</hi>) und Unterscheidung von <hi rend="italic">halgan þunresdæge</hi> vor Ostern d. i. Gründonnerstag bei Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Saints</hi> ed. Skeat n. 23b, l. 621, frz. <hi rend="italic">jeudi saint,</hi> Deutsch ‘guter Donnerstag’; Grotefend <hi rend="italic">Histor. Chronol.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B H cor. add ‘and’, So ‘or’, mistakenly. The processional days in the 5th week after Easter prepare for Christ’s Ascension; the cross, the Gospels and relics are carried round farmstead, cattle and fields; Anglo-Saxon homily of c. 1000 ed. M. Förster in <hi rend="italic">Morsbach Festg.</hi> 74. In Middle English, it is true, and today, <hi rend="italic">‘Holy Thursday’</hi> on its own means ‘Ascension’. In Anglo-Saxon, on the other hand, this meaning requires a closer specification (= Old French <hi rend="italic">joedi de rovoisons</hi> in Littré s. v. <hi rend="italic">jeudi</hi>) and distinction from <hi rend="italic">halgan þunresdæge</hi> before Easter, i.e. Maundy Thursday, in Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Saints</hi> ed. Skeat n. 23b, l. 621, French <hi rend="italic">jeudi saint,</hi> German ‘guter Donnerstag’; Grotefend <hi rend="italic">Histor. Chronol.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘alles dies [Verbrechen?]’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘all these [crimes?]’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-5.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Neben dem Ersatze’ [?] meint Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 41 gegen Schmid; an öffentliche Strafe denkt Pol Mai I 33. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Busse 10b; Fasten 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘In addition to the restitution’ [?] is Schreuer’s interpretation, <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 41, against Schmid; Pol Mai I 33 think of a public penalty. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Busse 10b; Fasten 11</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_5-5.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><label>Gehhol</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Geol</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_5-5.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><label>on</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊ <hi rend="italic">on</hi>. B &amp; Ld. <hi rend="italic">oððe</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_5-5.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><label>gehwelc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">æghwylc</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_5-5.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">According to Liebermann <hi rend="italic">Sunnanniht</hi> means ‘Sunday,’ which is no doubt correct for this passage. On the other hand two of the instances of the use of this word given in B. and T. clearly indicate the night between Saturday and Sunday.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_5-5.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">According to Liebermann the expression <hi rend="italic">ðone halgan Þunresdæg on Gangdagas</hi> is used in order to distinguish this day from Thursday in Holy Week. In some MSS (cf. p. 66, note 17) <hi rend="italic">and</hi> has been inserted (as a correction) between <hi rend="italic">dæg</hi> and <hi rend="italic">on</hi>, which would seem to show that the expression was not understood. Rogation Days are the three days before Ascension Day.</seg></note>
